# SYNOPSIS

```text
protocol todhchai.display.device.Display version 2
call outputs() -> [Output]
call edid(output: UInt32) throws(DisplayError) -> [UInt8]
call attach(vmo: Handle, width: UInt32, height: UInt32)
  throws(DisplayError) -> UInt32
call detach(image: UInt32)
call show(output: UInt32, image: UInt32) throws(DisplayError)
call flush(image: UInt32, damage: [Area]) throws(DisplayError)
event outputsChanged()
```

# DESCRIPTION

Protocol `todhchai.display.device.Display`, version 2, of library `DisplayDeviceIPC`, its messages in the one wire format (wire(6)).

| Method | Kind | Since | Ordinal |
| `outputs` | call | 1 | `0x75dfb05129d3f797` |
| `edid` | call | 1 | `0x57d2a87fba8c718f` |
| `attach` | call | 1 | `0x31b93b0e211f8d6e` |
| `detach` | call | 1 | `0x2902d387eda4f50c` |
| `show` | call | 1 | `0x379499d329fe2e16` |
| `flush` | call | 1 | `0x69bc682df7fa8377` |
| `outputsChanged` | event | 2 | `0x16c3fe95a4a148d5` |

: `edid`
  The output's EDID, if the device has one (empty otherwise).
: `attach`
  `vmo` (its first `width` × `height` pixels, rows packed) as an image
  the device reads; its id.
: `show`
  The output shows the image (0: nothing).
: `flush`
  The image's `damage` goes to the screen, when the call returns.
: `outputsChanged`
  A connector came or went, or a mode changed: ask `outputs` again.

